# Practical 3 – String Interpolation

## Aim

To create an Angular application that demonstrates string interpolation.

## Objective

To understand how string interpolation is used in Angular to display data from the component on the HTML page.

## Technologies Used

- Angular
- TypeScript
- HTML
- CSS
- Visual Studio Code

## 1. app.ts
import { Component, signal } from '@angular/core';
import { RouterOutlet } from '@angular/router';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  imports: [RouterOutlet],
  templateUrl: './app.html',
  styleUrl: './app.css'
})
export class App {
  
  name = 'Aarti Tonpe';
  course = 'M.Sc. Computer Science';
  college = 'MIT ACSC';

}
## 2. app.html
<div class="container">

  <h1>Student Information</h1>

  <p>My Name is: {{ name }}</p>

  <p>My Course is: {{ course }}</p>

  <p>My College is: {{ college }}</p>

</div> 
3. app.css
